{"name":"Burlap Grey","hex":"#81717e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burlap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very strong, coarse cloth, made from jute, flax, or hemp, and used to make sacks, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wrap or cover in burlap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burlap"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hessian fabric","blocks":[{"text":"Hessian, burlap in North America, or crocus in the Caribbean, is a woven fabric made of vegetable fibres: usually the skin of the jute plant, or sisal leaves. It is generally used for rough handling, such as to make sacks in which to ship farm products and sandbags, and for wrapping tree-root balls. However, this dense woven fabric, historically coarse, is also recently being produced in a more refined state—where it is known simply as jute—so as to provide an eco-friendly material for bags, rugs, and other products."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Burlap_%288963603095%29.jpg/330px-Burlap_%288963603095%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hessian_fabric","wikidata":"Q911285"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG/500px-Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG/500px-Sacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brazilian coffee beans in hessian gunny sacks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASacos_de_caf%C3%A9%2C_Casa_do_Bandeirante_2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg/500px-Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg/1280px-Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg/500px-Prepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Soldiers filling sandbags","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrepping_for_War_Fighter_DVIDS596004.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Rugaction.jpg/500px-Rugaction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Rugaction.jpg/500px-Rugaction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rug making on hessian","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARugaction.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Grey_Longhaired_Fem